#EXTM3U
# Curated local channels for the Lancaster / Harrisburg / Lebanon / York market
# (the Susquehanna Valley in south-central Pennsylvania) - the stations an
# antenna in Lancaster actually receives over the air:
#
#   WGAL 8.1  NBC  Lancaster      Hearst/Uplynk syndication (720p) + Local Now (720p)
#   WHP  21.1 CBS  Harrisburg     Sinclair live distribution (720p)
#   WPMT 43.1 FOX  York           Tegna One live (1080p)
#   WTXF 29   FOX  Philadelphia   Amagi (720p), the next market east
#
# WHTM 27.1 (ABC, Nexstar) and WITF 33.1 (PBS) are deliberately absent.
# abc27.com/watch-live mints a ~5-minute Anvato token for every playback
# (dcs4-live.mp.lura.live/server/play/<id>/manifest.m3u8?...&anvauth=tb=0~te=..., where
# te is ~5 min after the page load), and WITF's live player is Widevine DRM
# (static.drm.pbs.org). A playlist cannot refresh either token, so adding them
# would publish a link that is dead before the next scrape. Verified 2026-11-25.
#
# WGAL carries two doors because its syndication feed is not always up. The
# Uplynk/CloudFront address only generates a manifest when its full signed
# query travels with the request: the bare URL answered HTTP 504 ("Unable to
# obtain template playlist") on ten consecutive probes on 2026-11-25, while the
# signed address answered 200 with a full 720p ladder. The Local Now (Amagi)
# address of the same Hearst asset (90f3abbf...) answered 200 on every probe
# and is kept as the backup.
# The scraper keeps one as the channel and the other as "NBC Backups", so a
# player fails over to the door that answers; both feeds share the guide id, so
# the schedule survives the hop. Local Now's stitcher returns HTTP 400 unless
# its advertising parameters travel with the request, so that address is kept
# whole - it is long, and it is the only form that plays.
#
# Every URL in this file is re-checked end to end by scripts/scraper.py on every run,
# exactly like playlists/sources/ae-networks.m3u and playlists/sources/priority-channels.m3u:
# a feed that stops answering is dropped from the published playlists automatically.
#
# Adding a channel here also adds it to PremiumTV.m3u, PremiumTV_all.m3u and
# playlists/countries/USA.m3u on the next scrape, and its tvg-id is what the merged
# guide build (EPG/PremiumTV.xml) matches against the upstream guides.
